[b][size=6]StutterBegone[/size][/b]
Fixes stuttering when sweeping your mouse over shelves and other items, and reduces it in other UI screens.

[b][size=5]What it does[/size][/b]
The game draws all of its full-screen menus on top of one giant shared panel. Moving your mouse over the shelves makes that panel redraw ~100 times a second — that's what causes the stutter. StutterBegone splits the shared panel up so each screen is drawn on its own, meaning a change only redraws the one screen you're using. The hover stutter is gone and tooltips stay fully visible. Nothing is removed; every screen and item works exactly as before.

[b][size=5]Requirements[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]BepInEx 5[/b][/*]
[/list]
That's all — it runs on its own, alongside your other mods (EPL, ShopOS, …).

[b][size=5]Installation[/size][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download the latest version of this mod.[/*]
[*]Extract it into your game folder (the one that contains [font=monospace]Card Shop Simulator.exe[/font]) so that you end up with [font=monospace]BepInEx\plugins\StutterBegone\StutterBegone.dll[/font].[/*]
[*]Launch the game — it applies itself the next time the shop loads.[/*]
[/list]

[b][size=5]Configuration[/size][/b]
Everything works with the defaults. To tweak something, edit [font=monospace]BepInEx\config\dr.eldon.stutter.begone.cfg[/font] (in-game via a config manager, or the file directly):
[table][tr][th]Key[/th]
[th]Default[/th]
[th]What it does[/th]
[/tr]
[tr][td][font=monospace]Enabled[/font][/td]
[td][font=monospace]true[/font][/td]
[td]Turns the mod on or off.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][font=monospace]Verbose[/font][/td]
[td][font=monospace]false[/font][/td]
[td]Writes detailed lines to [font=monospace]LogOutput.log[/font]. Turn on when reporting a problem.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][font=monospace]ExcludeNames[/font][/td]
[td](empty)[/td]
[td]One or more screens to leave alone. Leave empty unless a screen breaks (see below).[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][font=monospace]ApplyDelayFrames[/font][/td]
[td][font=monospace]10[/font][/td]
[td]How long to wait after the shop loads before applying.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][font=monospace]BaseSortingOrder[/font][/td]
[td][font=monospace]100[/font][/td]
[td]Keeps the screens in their original stacking order. Leave as-is unless told otherwise.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][font=monospace]RescanCanvasesKey[/font][/td]
[td][font=monospace]None[/font][/td]
[td]Set a key, then press it if another mod's pop-up ends up hidden behind a screen — it brings that pop-up back on top.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

[b][size=5]If a screen breaks[/size][/b]
A couple of mods (EPL, ShopOS) find their screens in a way that moving them can upset. If a screen stops working, put its exact name in [font=monospace]ExcludeNames[/font] (separate several with commas) and restart. The usual suspects: [font=monospace]RestockItemScreen_Grp[/font], [font=monospace]RestockItemAddToCartScreen[/font], [font=monospace]RestockItemCheckoutScreen[/font]. When reporting a problem, enable [font=monospace]Verbose[/font] and attach [font=monospace]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/font].

[b][size=5]Uninstall[/size][/b]
Delete the folder [font=monospace]BepInEx\plugins\StutterBegone\[/font]. That's it — nothing is written to your saves or game files.
